OpenBLAS
========

The OpenBLAS library (http://xianyi.github.com/OpenBLAS/) is an excellent
optimized blas library. It is provided on most versions of Linux as a
pre-compiled library, and it is recommended to use that one. You can also
compile your own version, for example if the pre-compiled library is quite 
old and you want a newer one.

On macOS with Apple Silicon (arm64) it is recommended to use framework
Accelerate instead of OpenBLAS. See file README.macos_arm64.

Some notes for compiling your own version of OpenBLAS:

 * Edit the Makefile.rule file to set:
       FC = gfortran
       NO_SHARED = 1
       NO_CBLAS = 1
       NO_LAPACKE = 1
   to build a library optimized for your architecture.
   In addition you might set other options for your system. For example
     USE_THREAD = 0
   builds a sequential library (no threading) or
     USE_OPENMP = 1
   if the library is used with OpenMP.
       
 * Copy the resulting .a archives files (one lib and one link) to the lib
   directory of tfem:
     cp -d *.a <tfem-root>/lib
   and edit the Mdefs.mk file to find the blas library:

     LIBBLAS = -lopenblas

   for a sequential (single threaded) build of the library or

     LIBBLAS = -lopenblas -lpthread

   for a multi threaded build of the library.

 * Set the number of threads with

     export OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=n

   where n is the max number of threads. Notes:
     - if OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS is not set, OMP_NUM_THREADS is used instead. 
     - if OpenMP is used, the library must be built with USE_OPENMP = 1
       and OMP_NUM_THREADS must be used to set the maximum number of threads.
